From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Trieloff <lars@trieloff.net>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:00:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] exec: `--shell-grants`, and run the child in the cwd
 sent to the vault

`fnox exec --shell-grants -- cmd` sends `materialize {shellGrants: true,
path, argv, cwd}` (slicc-vault#9) instead of naming this configuration's
sealed secrets, which then keep their placeholders. Each name the vault
grants is set in the child's environment to its placeholder, from the
configuration when it holds the record and from `placeholder {name}`
otherwise, so the kernel can swap it at exec. The plain-value warning is
left out in this mode, which the agent's bash hook uses for every
command.

The child now also gets the cwd that went into the ticket explicitly,
so the kernel's binding of path, argv and cwd always matches what fnox
sent.

diff --git a/crates/fnox-core/src/sealed.rs b/crates/fnox-core/src/sealed.rs
index 9cf84738..3d85bf08 100644
--- a/crates/fnox-core/src/sealed.rs
+++ b/crates/fnox-core/src/sealed.rs
@@ -222,6 +222,16 @@ pub fn materialize(names: &[String], path: &str, argv: &[String], cwd: &str) ->
     )
 }
 
+pub fn materialize_shell_grants(path: &str, argv: &[String], cwd: &str) -> Result<Ticket> {
+    parse(
+        "materialize",
+        call(
+            "materialize",
+            json!({ "shellGrants": true, "path": path, "argv": argv, "cwd": cwd }),
+        )?,
+    )
+}
+
 pub enum Wait {
     Done(Request),
     Ended(Request),
